<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Space Grotesk — THE BRAND / FIGURE FACE (00-rules.md 3.4 / 5.1, decision D-2).

  Scope, exhaustively: the Display figure, the Chip label, the Numeric role, the
  wordmark, units, currency and Latin technical tokens (VLESS, Reality, WS, TCP,
  hosts, ports). NOTHING ELSE. Every Russian string is Golos Text (@font/golos_text).

  WHY THE SCOPE IS A HARD RULE, MEASURED. The vendored binary maps 735 codepoints
  and ZERO of them fall in U+0400-U+04FF. Not "few" — zero. So every Russian
  string that has ever carried android:fontFamily="@font/space_grotesk" has been a
  no-op that handed the glyphs to the platform fallback: Roboto on Android, some
  other face on desktop — the same screen set in three faces on three operating
  systems. That is the defect the two-face split exists to end, and it is why the
  face is a property of the ramp style and never of a layout.
  It DOES map: 0-9, the Latin alphabet, ₽ U+20BD, U+00A0 NBSP, U+2009 THIN SPACE
  and U+2007 FIGURE SPACE — everything 10-design-system.md 2.10 needs for numerals.

  WHAT THE BINARY CAN ACTUALLY DO (2.9.2's verification gate, settled by
  inspecting the file rather than by screenshotting it). spacegrotesk.ttf is a
  VARIABLE font: one axis, wght, min 300 / DEFAULT 300 / max 700, and
  usWeightClass 300. It ships a single Light default instance and no static masters.

  That measurement is the point of this file. Three <font> entries pointing at one
  variable file only tell Android which entry to MATCH; they do not tell the
  rasteriser which instance to CUT. So before this change every "700" brand run in
  the product was drawn at Light 300 while every style file looked correct — the
  exact failure 2.9.2 predicted. android:fontVariationSettings is what pins the
  instance, so each entry now carries it.

  API FLOOR, STATED HONESTLY. android:fontVariationSettings in a font resource is
  API 28+; app:fontVariationSettings is read by androidx.core's
  FontResourcesParserCompat and forwarded from API 26. On API 24-25 there is no
  variation path at all, so those two levels render Space Grotesk at its 300
  default and the Display/Chip weight difference is lost there. The fix is baked
  static instances (SpaceGrotesk-Medium/Bold.ttf) vendored as the fallback family;
  that is vendoring work, tracked as debt, and it changes nothing structural here —
  the three entries would simply point at three files, the way @font/golos_text
  already does.
-->
<font-family
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto">

    <!-- 400 — the axis floor is 300, so 'wght' 400 is the lightest honest
         instance this binary can cut. It exists so the family has a normal
         weight; no ramp role asks Space Grotesk for 400. -->
    <font
        android:font="@font/spacegrotesk"
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 400"
        android:fontWeight="400"
        app:font="@font/spacegrotesk"
        app:fontStyle="normal"
        app:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 400"
        app:fontWeight="400" />

    <!-- 500 — Chip labels and the Numeric role (D-4). -->
    <font
        android:font="@font/spacegrotesk"
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 500"
        android:fontWeight="500"
        app:font="@font/spacegrotesk"
        app:fontStyle="normal"
        app:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 500"
        app:fontWeight="500" />

    <!-- 700 — the Display figure and the wordmark. -->
    <font
        android:font="@font/spacegrotesk"
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 700"
        android:fontWeight="700"
        app:font="@font/spacegrotesk"
        app:fontStyle="normal"
        app:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 700"
        app:fontWeight="700" />

</font-family>
